A||N||2||LemonSky||Recall on parking brake in 1986 models||||5||
Z||000000||LemonSky||07-21-2000||09:40 PM||||I'm considering selling my 1986 SE6, and I can not, in good conscience, sell a car with a faulty emergency/parking brake. So I did some investigating on the internet to see how I might be able to fix it myself, and came across a site that indicated that in 1991, there was a recall on 1986 Fieros due to malfunctioning parking brakes. Excited that I may not have to pay anything to get them fixed, I was disappointed to see that it specified "manual transmissions" and I have an automatic. <P>Now, the car has been in our family for all 15 years, and my mom said it never worked. Being the cavalier she is, my mom just blew it off. When I received the car from her as a gift for painting her house (in the middle of Summer 1999, in the Georgia heat, that's how bad I wanted it) I was somewhat concerned, but I was happy to have it, and blew it off. But like I said in the beginning, I'm considering selling it but want to fix those brakes. Do you think Pontiac will still perform this service despite its automatic transmission? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Linx||07-22-2000||02:51 AM||||So- what's wrong with the brake?  I'm working on my SE as we speak...so Im gonna guess your cables have rusted thru, like mine.  A three piece cable sustem..and two of the cables pass thru the frame right behind the rear tires- they have lots of opportunity to get soaked, rust, and eventually seize.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||07-24-2000||07:56 AM||||Call 1-800-PMcares and give them the VIN and they will tell you if there are any outstanding recalls for your car.  I had my 85SE rear brakes re-done when I bought it with 109000 miles on it.<P>Tell me about the car.  I might be interested even with a non-working e-brake.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
